-- Conformance: mentioning a reserved prelude-namespace type is a checker error (Chapter 8, Section 8.4.1)
-- Tests: E154 — a type REFERENCE to a name in the prelude's reserved `Vera`
-- namespace is rejected where it is written (#1221).  The prelude injects the
-- aliases its combinators resolve through at code generation, never at the
-- checker, so a program that mentions one names a type the checker cannot see
-- and code generation can: the two partition this function's parameters
-- differently and the compiled export reads the wrong one.  Reserving the
-- namespace for references as well as declarations closes the divergence.
public fn f(@VeraOptionMapFn<Int, Bool> -> @Int)
  requires(true)
  ensures(true)
  effects(pure)
{
  0
}
